# Global AI rules for Event Planner Architecture

- Generate code only behind explicit interfaces or replaceable abstractions.
- Keep all persistence in memory. Do not add external databases, queues, SaaS APIs or hidden network calls.
- Follow TDD: create or update tests before changing service behavior.
- Keep business logic in `src/models`, `src/services`, `src/storage` and `src/utils`; React components may orchestrate but must not own domain rules.
- Use dependency injection for repositories, notification observers, conflict policies and strategies.
- Preserve GoF patterns already used in the project: Builder, Strategy and Observer.
- Every new branch of business logic must have unit tests and at least one edge-case test.
- CI reports must remain downloadable from workflow artifacts.
